@0    = ~(sigh) I sense where this is going.~
@1    = ~<CHARNAME>, I do not need to tell you that if you attempt to do the first task, our alliance will be over - and we will be enemies.~
@2    = ~<CHARNAME>, this was a mistake. You helped me, so I'll refrain from murdering you in your sleep tonight, but will wait until we cross blades next time we meet - probably in a guild fight. It's a pity we lose you to our enemy, but that is how life goes. I can't say 'Farewell' because we are enemies now, but I can say 'Take care'.~
@3    = ~Well, well, you shouldn't start a business relation with a lie, man. 'Malficus' surely is not your first name. Maybe more of a hint as to what to expect from you?~
@4    = ~Oh, it's not the name my *parents* gave me, but that wasn't the question, was it? And I am a sincere businessman, will you just listen.~
@5    = ~No, *you* did not follow us, or I would know. But I see where this is going. Who are you working for?~
@6    = ~Oh, but do not tangle yourself up in distrust before even listening to my offer. I am a sincere businessman, will you just listen.~
@7    = ~There, at least, he is right.~
@8    = ~<CHARNAME>, you aren't that naive to think that this is something this man wants to be done for himself, are you? I bet with you that he has a client who paid him a lot of gold for this errand to be performed, and now he lets you do it - without having to pay for it!~
@9    = ~Well, aren't you a suspicious one. I *am* paying, in the end - because I will have to refund the lowered cost of your friend's ship voyage out of my own pocket, have I not?~
@10   = ~Hmm, I am not sure I got this right, <CHARNAME>. I expected you to go for Ireniucs, now you are planning to... what, take a leave?~
@11   = ~Yep. I think I earned myself a timeout.~
@12   = ~You are welcome to go, if you don't like it.~
@13   = ~I don't like it, that is true.~
@14   = ~Nevertheless, I will go with you. Why? Because I am convinced that if you don't go to Irenicus, he will come for you. And that is all that matters.~
@15   = ~<CHARNAME>, I have to warn you about this Malficus.~
@16   = ~Do you know who he is working for?~
@17   = ~Why?~
@18   = ~Husam, I will take his offer to leave this place, no matter who he is working for.~
@19   = ~Husam, I already paid him to leave this place, no matter who he is working for.~
@20   = ~That is the reason why I have to warn you.~
@21   = ~We couldn't track who he is working for.~
@22   = ~Oha. That shady?~
@23   = ~What's the problem, then?~
@24   = ~And that is a bad thing?~
@25   = ~You don't understand.~
@26   = ~That shady, indeed.~
@27   = ~Yes, very bad.~
@28   = ~See, I had several thieves observe him and follow him and his clients. And we couldn't track *any* connection to any bigger organization in the city. No, this is not a good sign. Because the kind of operations this man pulls off - he *can't* do them on his own, <CHARNAME>. Someone is helping him, and they are hiding their tracks way too well.~
@29   = ~Who do you think could be behind him?~
@30   = ~What do you suggest?~
@31   = ~Husam, I don't care. He seems trustworthy enough to get us on a boat, and we aren't exactly helpless, overall.~
@32   = ~Difficult to say... If I had to guess, I would say Night Knives. Not a belated greeting from Mae'Var, I don't think he was that important there in the end. But they would be an organization that could pull something like this off, and their desire for secrecy is well known.~
@33   = ~Something is very, very off with this man. But as long as we don't know whether it has anything to do with *you*, all we can do is keep our eyes and ears open for nasty surprises.~
@34   = ~We are already preparing to leave with his ship, so there is little we can do other than to keep our eyes and ears open for nasty surprises - and hope that the secrecy of his organisation has nothing to do with *you*.~
@35   = ~Bodhi! So this Malficus worked for our rival guild, after all - and it *was* addressed against you. Cursed be my naivite - the thought of even considering the possibility that it might have nothing to do with you brings tears of shame to my eyes.~
@36   = ~Well, yeah, guess I have to accept that I am a very wanted person.~
@37   = ~You haven't been a great help in this, indeed.~
@38   = ~Oh well, I guess we can look for this Spellhold, now that we are here already.~
@39   = ~The persons responsible for this better watch out.~
@40   = ~One good thing came out of this, though. Now we are nearer Irenicus that I had dared to hope when going for this journey.~
@41   = ~Well - I wasn't the one making the deal, <CHARNAME>.~
@42   = ~Ha! The irony of life. I trusted in Irenicus coming for you if you don't go for him. I didn't consider *you* being brought to *him* as an option.~
@43   = ~Husam, would you please tell Inspector Brega that the accusations are true?~
@44   = ~<CHARNAME>, please - of course I will second what you said, but Chief Inspector Brega is a very busy man. He surely can't know every *honest and normal* citizen of this city.~
